WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.118
Present:

2
00:00:01.398 --> 00:00:02.827
Routines and Right Now.

3
00:00:03.107 --> 00:00:06.563
Day 6 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the English phase.

4
00:00:08.313 --> 00:00:09.337
The key idea.

5
00:00:09.617 --> 00:00:17.724
Today's goal: talk about your daily routine (present simple) and what's happening now (present continuous), and ask questions with both.

6
00:00:19.074 --> 00:00:19.927
Part 1.

7
00:00:20.207 --> 00:00:21.786
Two presents, two jobs.

8
00:00:23.036 --> 00:00:24.380
Here is a quick table:

9
00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.857
Present simple, and Present continuous.

10
00:00:27.137 --> 00:00:27.991
Use for.

11
00:00:28.271 --> 00:00:30.745
Present simple: habits, routines, facts.

12
00:00:31.025 --> 00:00:34.268
Present continuous: right now, these days, temporary.

13
00:00:34.548 --> 00:00:35.316
Form.

14
00:00:35.596 --> 00:00:36.577
Present simple:

15
00:00:36.857 --> 00:00:38.031
I work, She works.

16
00:00:38.311 --> 00:00:39.569
Present continuous:

17
00:00:39.849 --> 00:00:41.513
I am working, She is working.

18
00:00:41.793 --> 00:00:42.753
Key words.

19
00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:46.383
Present simple: always, usually, every day, on Mondays.

20
00:00:46.663 --> 00:00:50.460
Present continuous: now, right now, at the moment, today, this week.

21
00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:51.615
Example.

22
00:00:51.895 --> 00:00:52.876
Present simple:

23
00:00:53.156 --> 00:00:54.671
I take the metro to work.

24
00:00:54.951 --> 00:00:56.209
Present continuous:

25
00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:59.540
I'm taking an auto today because the metro is closed.

26
00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:01.765
Part 2.

27
00:01:02.045 --> 00:01:03.026
Present simple.

28
00:01:04.276 --> 00:01:05.620
Here is a quick table:

29
00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:08.119
Positive, and Negative, and Question.

30
00:01:08.399 --> 00:01:09.721
I start work at 9.

31
00:01:10.001 --> 00:01:10.897
Negative:

32
00:01:11.177 --> 00:01:12.692
I don't start work at 9.

33
00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:13.847
Question:

34
00:01:14.127 --> 00:01:15.556
Do you start work at 9?

35
00:01:15.836 --> 00:01:17.095
She lives in Chennai.

36
00:01:17.375 --> 00:01:18.271
Negative:

37
00:01:18.551 --> 00:01:20.023
She doesn't live in Chennai.

38
00:01:20.303 --> 00:01:21.177
Question:

39
00:01:21.457 --> 00:01:22.801
Does she live in Chennai?

40
00:01:23.081 --> 00:01:24.575
The shop closes at 10.

41
00:01:24.855 --> 00:01:25.751
Negative:

42
00:01:26.031 --> 00:01:27.652
The shop doesn't close at 10.

43
00:01:27.932 --> 00:01:28.807
Question:

44
00:01:29.087 --> 00:01:30.516
When does the shop close?

45
00:01:31.866 --> 00:01:37.754
Spelling: work, then works, watch, then watches, go, then goes, study, then studies, have, then has.

46
00:01:38.034 --> 00:01:45.437
How often: always (100%), then usually, then often, then sometimes, then rarely, then never (0%).

47
00:01:45.717 --> 00:01:50.197
Position: before the main verb (I usually walk), after be (I'm always late).

48
00:01:51.547 --> 00:01:52.443
Part 3.

49
00:01:52.723 --> 00:01:53.981
Present continuous.

50
00:01:55.231 --> 00:01:56.575
Here is a quick table:

51
00:01:56.855 --> 00:01:59.074
Positive, and Negative, and Question.

52
00:01:59.354 --> 00:02:00.954
I'm working from home today.

53
00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:02.130
Negative:

54
00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:03.797
I'm not working today.

55
00:02:04.077 --> 00:02:04.951
Question:

56
00:02:05.231 --> 00:02:06.490
Are you working today?

57
00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:08.242
He's talking to the client.

58
00:02:08.522 --> 00:02:09.418
Negative:

59
00:02:09.698 --> 00:02:11.319
He isn't talking to the client.

60
00:02:11.599 --> 00:02:12.474
Question:

61
00:02:12.754 --> 00:02:14.055
Who is he talking to?

62
00:02:14.335 --> 00:02:15.679
They're building a new app.

63
00:02:15.959 --> 00:02:16.855
Negative:

64
00:02:17.135 --> 00:02:18.287
They aren't building it.

65
00:02:18.567 --> 00:02:19.442
Question:

66
00:02:19.722 --> 00:02:20.874
What are they building?

67
00:02:22.224 --> 00:02:22.971
Warning:

68
00:02:23.251 --> 00:02:30.141
Some verbs are not used in -ing (state verbs). know, understand, want, like, need, believe, own, belong, seem.

69
00:02:30.421 --> 00:02:31.531
I am knowing him.

70
00:02:31.811 --> 00:02:33.176
I am having two kids.

71
00:02:33.456 --> 00:02:34.373
I know him.

72
00:02:34.653 --> 00:02:35.827
I have two kids.

73
00:02:37.177 --> 00:02:38.094
Part 4.

74
00:02:38.374 --> 00:02:40.806
Your daily routine: useful sentences.

75
00:02:42.056 --> 00:02:44.680
I wake up at 6:30 and go for a walk.

76
00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:48.523
I have breakfast at 8 and leave for work at 8:45.

77
00:02:48.803 --> 00:02:52.323
I usually take the metro; it takes about 35 minutes.

78
00:02:52.603 --> 00:02:54.352
We have a stand-up meeting at 10.

79
00:02:54.632 --> 00:02:57.789
I get back home around 7 and spend time with my kids.

80
00:02:58.069 --> 00:03:01.248
On weekends, I play badminton and visit my parents.

81
00:03:02.598 --> 00:03:03.558
Part 5.

82
00:03:03.838 --> 00:03:06.099
Conversation: catching up with a friend.

83
00:03:07.349 --> 00:03:09.376
Here is how the conversation goes.

84
00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:10.445
Hey!

85
00:03:10.725 --> 00:03:12.325
What are you doing these days?

86
00:03:12.605 --> 00:03:15.016
I'm working on a new project at work.

87
00:03:15.296 --> 00:03:17.152
We're building a delivery app.

88
00:03:17.432 --> 00:03:18.477
Nice!

89
00:03:18.757 --> 00:03:20.293
Do you still work from home?

90
00:03:20.573 --> 00:03:21.853
Not every day.

91
00:03:22.133 --> 00:03:24.608
I go to the office three days a week now.

92
00:03:24.888 --> 00:03:26.168
How do you get there?

93
00:03:27.518 --> 00:03:29.118
The conversation continues.

94
00:03:29.398 --> 00:03:31.318
I usually take the metro.

95
00:03:31.598 --> 00:03:36.099
But this week I'm driving, because the metro line is closed for repairs.

96
00:03:36.379 --> 00:03:38.214
And are you still playing badminton?

97
00:03:38.494 --> 00:03:40.755
Yes, I play every Saturday morning.

98
00:03:41.035 --> 00:03:42.443
Do you want to join us?

99
00:03:42.723 --> 00:03:43.385
Sure!

100
00:03:43.665 --> 00:03:45.158
What time do you start?

101
00:03:45.438 --> 00:03:46.889
We start at seven.

102
00:03:47.169 --> 00:03:48.961
I'll send you the location.

103
00:03:50.311 --> 00:03:51.249
Part 6.

104
00:03:51.529 --> 00:03:52.447
Practice.

105
00:03:53.697 --> 00:03:54.337
1.

106
00:03:54.617 --> 00:03:56.003
Simple or continuous?

107
00:03:56.283 --> 00:03:57.478
She (work) at a bank.

108
00:03:57.758 --> 00:03:58.462
2.

109
00:03:58.742 --> 00:03:59.403
Look!

110
00:03:59.683 --> 00:04:00.601
It (rain).

111
00:04:00.881 --> 00:04:01.627
3.

112
00:04:01.907 --> 00:04:03.550
I (not like) long meetings.

113
00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:05.089
We (have) lunch now.

114
00:04:05.369 --> 00:04:06.563
Can I call you back?

115
00:04:06.843 --> 00:04:07.611
5.

116
00:04:07.891 --> 00:04:09.939
The train usually (leave) on time.

117
00:04:11.289 --> 00:04:12.207
Success:

118
00:04:12.487 --> 00:04:17.265
Answers. works 2. is raining 3. don't like 4. are having 5. leaves.

119
00:04:18.615 --> 00:04:19.319
2.

120
00:04:19.599 --> 00:04:20.687
Make questions.

121
00:04:20.967 --> 00:04:23.143
(you or usually or get up or when) 2.

122
00:04:23.423 --> 00:04:25.706
(he or work or today or from home) 3.

123
00:04:25.986 --> 00:04:27.501
(what or you or do or now).

124
00:04:28.851 --> 00:04:29.768
Success:

125
00:04:30.048 --> 00:04:30.901
Answers.

126
00:04:31.181 --> 00:04:32.589
When do you usually get up?

127
00:04:32.869 --> 00:04:33.573
2.

128
00:04:33.853 --> 00:04:35.432
Is he working from home today?

129
00:04:35.712 --> 00:04:36.459
3.

130
00:04:36.739 --> 00:04:37.955
What are you doing now?

131
00:04:39.305 --> 00:04:40.051
3.

132
00:04:40.331 --> 00:04:41.547
Fix the mistakes.

133
00:04:41.827 --> 00:04:46.521
He go to gym daily. / I am understanding. / She is work in Wipro.

134
00:04:47.871 --> 00:04:48.788
Success:

135
00:04:49.068 --> 00:04:49.921
Answers.

136
00:04:50.201 --> 00:04:54.980
He goes to the gym every day. / I understand. / She works at Wipro.

137
00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:57.269
Part 7.

138
00:04:57.549 --> 00:04:58.594
Speak today.

139
00:04:59.844 --> 00:05:03.172
Describe your daily routine aloud in 8 sentences.

140
00:05:03.452 --> 00:05:06.759
Tell someone what you're working on this week (present continuous).

141
00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:08.084
Ask a colleague:

142
00:05:08.364 --> 00:05:10.007
What are you working on these days?

143
00:05:11.357 --> 00:05:12.893
That's the end of this lesson.

144
00:05:13.173 --> 00:05:17.823
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

145
00:05:18.103 --> 00:05:24.226
